  body: |
    # Household in the ESA(IR) source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The guidance describes a household through domestic life and ties between people, distinguishing sharing a dwelling from membership of the same household.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 43001 limits this family and household exercise to ESA(IR). The source says the same exercise is not needed for ESA(Cont). A shared address, temporary separation or family label alone does not decide household membership.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 43001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ede1a10d3bf7f2c9a297c32/dmgch43.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 43027, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ede1a10d3bf7f2c9a297c32/dmgch43.pdf#page=10)
    - [DMG 43051, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ede1a10d3bf7f2c9a297c32/dmgch43.pdf#page=15)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:28.912702Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

